An $x$-intercept where the curve **cuts** gives the factor $(x-a)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.4:3.8,smooth,variable=\x,samples=70] plot ({\x},{0.5*(\x-1.2)+0.05*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)});
\fill (1.2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (1.2,0) {$x=a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An $x$-intercept where the curve **bounces** gives $(x-a)^{2}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.4:3.8,smooth,variable=\x,samples=70] plot ({\x},{0.4*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)});
\fill (1.2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (1.2,0) {$x=a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An $x$-intercept where the curve **inflects** along the axis gives $(x-a)^{3}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.4,0)--(4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.4:3.8,smooth,variable=\x,samples=70] plot ({\x},{0.16*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)});
\fill (1.2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (1.2,0) {$x=a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The roots fix the equation only up to a constant multiple $k$, since infinitely many curves share the same intercepts.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4.6,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.6:3.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=80] plot ({\x},{0.10*(\x+2.4)*(\x+0.4)*(\x-2.4)});
\draw[thick,red,dashed,<->,domain=-3.2:3.1,smooth,variable=\x,samples=80] plot ({\x},{0.22*(\x+2.4)*(\x+0.4)*(\x-2.4)});
\draw[thick,green!50!black,dashdotted,<->,domain=-3.8:3.8,smooth,variable=\x,samples=80] plot ({\x},{0.045*(\x+2.4)*(\x+0.4)*(\x-2.4)});
\fill (-2.4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (-2.4,0) {$a$};
\fill (-0.4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (-0.4,0) {$b$};
\fill (2.4,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below right] at (2.4,0) {$c$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

